{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Guide me</b> — This verse is weighty. The sense: he asks that HaShem aid him on the path of truth until he becomes practiced [in it]. This is the sense of 'and teach me,' like the practice of an animal, as in 'an untrained calf.'" "And the sense of <b>my Elohim of salvation</b>: that He save him from anything that would prevent him from walking on the path of truth, for I have none to hope in besides You."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:30.876648663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}